@*
    A consumer-shaped component inside a form: it does work whenever its parameters are set, and
    says how often that has happened. Its parameter is an object, which Blazor cannot prove
    unchanged, so every render of the markup around it re-sets its parameters, as every render does
    for a component handed a model, a list or a callback. The count rides on an attribute rather
    than in text, so the counter's own render adds or removes no node under the form.
*@
<span id="parameter-sets" data-parameter-sets="@_parameterSets"></span>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public object? Token { get; set; }

    private int _parameterSets;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        _parameterSets++;
    }
}
